<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>true</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Testing">
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.v3" Version="3.2.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The only runtime dependency in src/, and the narrowest form of it: ModelContextProtocol.Core
       rather than ModelContextProtocol, which costs four transitive packages on net10.0 instead of
       about twelve and brings no generic host. Justified in DECISIONS.md D-0019 as docs/PRODUCT.md law 3.9
       requires. Keypaste.Core — the vault and crypto path — still has none. -->
  <ItemGroup Label="MCP bridge">
    <PackageVersion Include="ModelContextProtocol.Core" Version="1.4.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- The desktop shell (Stage 4.1). This is the largest single change to this repository's
       supply chain — four direct packages and roughly twenty transitive ones, in the process that
       holds the unlocked vault — so docs/PRODUCT.md law 3.9 governs it and DECISIONS.md D-0044 carries the
       written justification.

       What Avalonia is trusted with: rendering the window and delivering the keystrokes of the
       master password. What it is NOT trusted with: it never touches the KDBX file, never derives
       a key, never reads the audit log and never opens a socket. Keypaste.Core still has no
       PackageReference at all, and that is the line that matters.

       Avalonia.Diagnostics is deliberately absent. It has no 12.x release, and a runtime
       visual-tree inspector attached to a process holding an unlocked vault is not something to
       ship even in Debug. CommunityToolkit.Mvvm is absent for the reason D-0028 gave for writing a
       TOML parser by hand: sixty lines of INotifyPropertyChanged is not a dependency's worth of
       work. -->
  <ItemGroup Label="Desktop app">
    <PackageVersion Include="Avalonia" Version="12.1.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Avalonia.Desktop" Version="12.1.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Avalonia.Themes.Fluent" Version="12.1.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Avalonia.Fonts.Inter" Version="12.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Avalonia.Headless only, not Avalonia.Headless.XUnit: a spike proved HeadlessUnitTestSession
       drives xunit.v3 directly under this repository's Microsoft.Testing.Platform runner, so the
       integration package buys an attribute and costs a dependency. One session per process — a
       second throws on the 'avares' URI parser — so the test project shares one static session. -->
  <ItemGroup Label="Desktop app tests">
    <PackageVersion Include="Avalonia.Headless" Version="12.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
